<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Classpath-only pom for the dmn-check harness. Nothing here is part of the L4
  build: `run.sh` uses it exclusively to resolve a classpath into $TMPDIR, and the
  jars never enter the repo.

  WHAT dmn-check IS. red6/dmn-check, https://github.com/red6/dmn-check, Apache-2.0
  (the licence block of the 1.4.0 parent pom on Maven Central says so). A set of
  static analyses over a DMN file's STRUCTURE: duplicate, conflicting and shadowed
  rules, missing ids and names, input/output type declarations, entries whose
  FEEL does not match the declared type, aggregation misuse, and requirement-graph
  shape. It reads the file with Camunda 7's camunda-dmn-model and never executes
  anything. It is therefore a third kind of evidence beside etc/validate-dmn.mjs
  (is the XML well-formed DMN 1.3?) and etc/camunda-dmn-check (does a Camunda 8
  engine load and evaluate it?).

  VERSION IS PINNED, and so is every transitive jar: jars.sha256 holds the
  SHA-256 of each file on the resolved classpath, and run.sh refuses to run if
  one differs. 1.4.0 is the latest release on Maven Central (maven-metadata.xml,
  lastUpdated 2026-07-15) and its parent pom sets java.version to 21, so the
  harness needs JDK 21+. Bumping the version means regenerating jars.sha256
  (README, "Bumping the pin").

  dmn-check-cli is the artifact the project ships as a command line; it pulls in
  dmn-check-plugin-base, -validators and -core. The harness drives the validators
  from its own small main class (src/main/java/DmnCheckRun.java) rather than
  through the CLI's, because the CLI prints nothing for a file with no findings,
  cannot say which validator produced a finding, and names no file when one
  cannot be read. README, "Why a driver and not the CLI".

  Keep this classpath apart from etc/camunda-dmn-check's and etc/kie-dmn-check's.
  dmn-check carries Camunda 7's camunda-dmn-model 7.24.0, and the pom in
  etc/camunda-dmn-check records that Camunda 7 and Camunda 8 artifacts must never
  share a classpath. Nobody has tried merging these; separate directories make
  the question moot.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <groupId>com.legalese.l4</groupId>
  <artifactId>dmn-check-harness</artifactId>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>
  <properties>
    <dmncheck.version>1.4.0</dmncheck.version>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
  </properties>
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>de.redsix</groupId>
      <artifactId>dmn-check-cli</artifactId>
      <version>${dmncheck.version}</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <!-- The plugin run.sh invokes, pinned so that "mvn dependency:build-classpath"
           does not mean a different plugin on every machine. 3.7.0 is what
           resolved on 2026-10-30. Its jars run BEFORE jars.sha256 is checked, so this
           is a version pin and not a checksum pin; README, "What is not verified". -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-dependency-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>3.7.0</version>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
